-- #955 (2026-10-28): walk links + paths for the travel nodes that 2026_10_28_00.sql left without any (playerbots DB).
-- Follow-up of 2026_10_28_00.sql. That file moved stale flight-master / innkeeper nodes onto their MoP NPC spawns and, for
-- the five flight masters that moved more than 300 yd (39 Talrendis Point, 211 Stonetalon Peak, 271 Marshals Refuge,
-- 646 Bloodvenom Post, 669 Feathermoon Stronghold), deleted their walk links (type 1) because the stored paths ended at
-- the old position. This file re-creates them, removes two stale start-zone inn nodes and links the ship decks:
--  * 39 / 211 / 271 / 646 / 669: walk links + paths in both directions to every node of the same map within 2000 yd that
--    the navmesh connects (the node itself is first snapped onto the nearest walkable poly of a main navmesh component,
--    <= 12 yd, hence the absolute UPDATEs of x / y / z below).
--  * 620 (Camp Narache innkeeper) and 629 (Shadowglen innkeeper) are DELETED with every link and path row to / from them
--    (all types, both directions). Their MoP innkeepers (Innkeeper Kauth guid 260070, Innkeeper Keldamyr guid 276902) are
--    already covered by node 215 (Bloodhoof Village innkeeper) and node 664 (Dolanaar innkeeper), which stand exactly on
--    them, so moving 620 / 629 there would only make 1 yd duplicates. They were the only connectors of the start nodes
--    62 (Red Cloud Mesa spirithealer) and 3 (Night Elf start), so those two get walk links + paths of their own to the
--    nodes the navmesh connects (including 215 and 664), same generator and AC crop.
--  * 1962 / 1968 (Darnassus boat decks, map 1, z 0, only a type-3 transport link): the deck points are on the navmesh
--    (water surface poly, 0.27 yd below), like the Stormwind harbor deck 2032, so they get ordinary walk links
--    (to 1680 Darnassus portal, each other and Rutheran Village). The decks are unchanged.
-- Generator (offline, same model as 2026_10_27_02.sql / #847 lane X: AC TravelNodeMap::generateWalkPaths + removeUselessPaths):
-- (not shipped) TG_WORKERS=4 python gen955.py ; python emit955.py ; python verify955b.py
--    (targets = the nine nodes 39 211 271 646 669 62 3 1962 1968, partners = every node of the map within 2000 yd,
--    tg_work.walk_job = Detour A* with the bot filter over the 5.4.8 mmaps of the extracted 5.4.8 client data,
--    points every <= 15 yd, AC calculateCost values, tg_crop.crop = isUselessLink; tg_* modules from
-- (not shipped).
-- Result: 218 walk links (type 1), 342 candidate pairs walked, 83 without a navmesh path, 288 cropped by isUselessLink; 2 nodes deleted.
--   per node (links out + in): 39: 37, 211: 22, 271: 25, 646: 27, 669: 33, 62: 41, 3: 25, 1962: 4, 1968: 6
-- Every row is linked / calculated = 1. Idempotent: absolute UPDATEs, DELETEs by id / pair before every INSERT.
-- Apply after 2026_10_28_00.sql. Undo: restore the previous x / y / z (old value in each UPDATE comment), DELETE the pairs of
--   the first DELETE pair, and re-insert nodes 620 / 629 with their links from the pre-file DB state.

